From: Alex Scotti <alexscotti@gmail.com>
Subject: vvc1: keep the CPU frame copy coherent with the decoder and the display

For progressive VC-1 the driver copies every decoded frame from the decode
buffer into one of 32 copy buffers with memcpy (033e2658, "use backup frame
table ... ucode higher than 3.49"). Both buffers are CMA memory reached
through codec_mm_phys_to_virt(), which is the cacheable kernel linear map,
and the copy did no cache maintenance at all: the VDEC had written the source
by DMA and the VPU reads the copy by DMA, but the CPU read the source through
whatever it still held in its caches from copying that same buffer four frames
earlier, and left the copy sitting in cache. It also handed the decode buffer
back to the firmware (VC1_BUFFERIN) before taking the copy.

On an S905X5M (Ugoos AM9 Pro, Cortex-A510) that shows as short horizontal
lines on moving VC-1 pictures and never on a paused frame: each line is one
stale 64-byte cache line, a 32x2 pixel patch of an older frame in the 32x32
block-mode canvas. Captured off the box with the stock driver in 10 of 120
frames of Beerfest; none in 120 with this change. MPEG-2 has no such copy and
is clean in hardware. H.264 and HEVC never touch this path.

Invalidate the source range before the memcpy, write the copy back to DDR
after it, and release the decode buffer only once the copy has been taken.

---
--- a/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/vc1/vvc1.c
+++ b/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/vc1/vvc1.c
@@ -1187,14 +1187,25 @@
 
 			hw->vfbuf_use[buffer_index]++;
 
+			{
+				void *dst = decoder_bmmu_box_get_virt_addr(mm_blk_handle, buffer_index);
+				void *src = decoder_bmmu_box_get_virt_addr(mm_blk_handle, vf->index);
+				int size = decoder_bmmu_box_get_mem_size(mm_blk_handle, vf->index);
+
+				/* The decoder wrote this frame by DMA: drop any stale CPU
+				 * cache lines before reading it, and write the copy back
+				 * to DDR before the display (also DMA) reads it. */
+				codec_mm_dma_flush(src, size, DMA_FROM_DEVICE);
+				memcpy(dst, src, size);
+				codec_mm_dma_flush(dst, size, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
+			}
+
+			/* Hand the decode buffer back to the firmware only after
+			 * the copy has been taken from it. */
 			if (--hw->vfbuf_use[vf->index] == 0) {
 				WRITE_VREG(VC1_BUFFERIN, ~(1 << vf->index));
 				hw->buf_use[vf->index]--;
 			}
-
-			memcpy(decoder_bmmu_box_get_virt_addr(mm_blk_handle, buffer_index),
-			       decoder_bmmu_box_get_virt_addr(mm_blk_handle, vf->index),
-			       decoder_bmmu_box_get_mem_size(mm_blk_handle, vf->index));
 			vf->canvas0Addr = vf->canvas1Addr = index2canvas(buffer_index);
 			if (is_support_vdec_canvas()) {
 				vf->canvas0Addr = vf->canvas1Addr = -1;
